# PART 4 — STANDARD AGENT IDENTITY CONTRACT

Every agent must have a uniquely identifiable configuration.

### Required identity fields

| Field | Description |
|---|---|
| agent_id | Unique identifier, AGT-001 through AGT-029 |
| agent_name | Official agent name |
| agent_version | Current agent specification/configuration version |
| registry_version | Master registry version |
| contract_version | Supported contract version |
| category_id | Associated primary category |
| category_name | Official category name |
| agent_role | Specialized business role |
| mission | Agent's main purpose |
| lifecycle_status | Draft, Approved, Active, Suspended or Retired |
| configuration_status | Configuration validation state |
| capabilities | Authorized capability references |
| restrictions | Agent-specific restrictions |

### Identity validation rules

- Agent IDs must be unique.
- Agent names must match Step 04.
- Category association must match Step 05.
- An agent must not claim another agent's identity.
- An unapproved agent must not be treated as active.
- A retired or suspended agent must not receive normal production requests.
- Agent identity must be verified by the trusted backend, not accepted solely from user-supplied request data.

The registry status and deployment status must remain separate.

An agent may be finalized in documentation while still not being implemented or deployed.

