# PART 22 — TESTING AND VALIDATION SPECIFICATION

Prepare a test plan for the future implementation.

## 22.1 Contract Validation Tests

- Valid request.
- Missing required field.
- Invalid contract version.
- Invalid agent ID.
- Invalid category mapping.
- Invalid tenant reference.
- Invalid execution mode.
- Invalid request payload.
- Unsupported attachment type.

## 22.2 Authentication and Authorization Tests

- Authenticated authorized user.
- Unauthenticated user.
- User without business access.
- User with insufficient permissions.
- Suspended agent.
- Unapproved agent.
- Unauthorized tool request.

## 22.3 Tenant Isolation Tests

- Tenant A cannot read Tenant B inventory.
- Tenant A cannot read Tenant B conversations.
- Tenant A cannot access Tenant B memory.
- Tenant A cannot execute tools on Tenant B resources.
- One business cannot modify another business's records.
- Context references cannot be reused across unauthorized tenants.

## 22.4 Runtime Tests

- Successful synchronous execution.
- Successful asynchronous execution.
- Streaming interruption.
- Tool timeout.
- Model-provider failure.
- Context retrieval failure.
- Agent unavailable.
- User cancellation.
- Runtime cancellation.
- Duplicate write request.
- Retry after temporary failure.

## 22.5 Safety Tests

- Prompt injection attempt.
- Unauthorized financial action.
- Unauthorized stock adjustment.
- Malicious uploaded content.
- Cross-agent access attempt.
- Sensitive-data disclosure attempt.
- False tool-success claim.
- Invalid approval reference.

## 22.6 29-Agent Compliance Tests

Each agent must pass:
- Identity validation.
- Category mapping validation.
- Contract validation.
- Capability boundary validation.
- Tool permission validation.
- Tenant isolation validation.
- Response schema validation.
- Error handling validation.

A single agent passing does not prove that all 29 agents are compliant.

